# Cloudflare Pages headers.
#
# ============================================================================
# THIS FILE CURRENTLY KEEPS THE WHOLE SITE OUT OF EVERY SEARCH INDEX.
#
# DELETE THE X-Robots-Tag BLOCK WHEN momentaura.store IS CONNECTED.
# Leaving it in place after go-live makes the real shop unfindable, silently,
# on a site whose whole problem is being found and believed. Nothing here can
# detect that: the header is correct today and wrong the moment the domain is
# connected, and the only difference between the two is a DNS change that
# happens outside this repo. verify.mjs prints a note on every build for as
# long as this block exists, which is the only reminder there is.
# ============================================================================
#
# The site deploys to the .pages.dev URL only. momentaura.store is registered
# and owned, and stays unconnected until there is real stock and photography.
# Google forming a first impression of a shop with five out-of-stock products
# and kraft placeholders is a cost that is paid once and is hard to undo, and
# a first impression is the entire subject of this build.
#
# canonical and the sitemap already name momentaura.store, which is correct and
# not a contradiction: they describe where the site lives, this describes
# whether to index what is being served. noindex is what makes the mismatch
# harmless in the meantime — a crawler that reads a canonical pointing at a host
# that is not serving would otherwise have nowhere to go.
#
# X-Robots-Tag is used rather than Disallow in robots.txt on purpose. Disallow
# stops a crawler reading the page, which also stops it reading a noindex, so a
# URL discovered from a link elsewhere can still be listed. noindex is read and
# obeyed.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache

# ============================================================================
# CACHING
#
# Two rules, and the difference between them is whether the filename changes
# when the bytes do.
#
# HTML is `no-cache`, which is not `no-store`. no-store forbids keeping a copy
# and makes every visit a full download, which on a metered Kenyan mobile
# bundle is the buyer paying for the same 21KB again to read the same page.
# no-cache keeps the copy and revalidates it, so an unchanged page costs a 304
# and a few hundred bytes.
#
# It is not a max-age either. A short max-age serves a stale page for its
# duration, and what is on these pages is stock, price and dispatch — the
# checkable facts this whole site is built on. Selling something the catalogue
# marked sold out four minutes ago is exactly the vendor behaviour the buyer
# arrived expecting. Revalidate every time; the page is small and the answer is
# usually 304.
#
# Everything below is content-addressed and therefore immutable for a year.
# `immutable` is a promise that these exact bytes never change at this exact
# URL, and it is only keepable because the hash is in the filename:
#
#   /img/crew-tee-1-800.7321b82b.webp
#   /_astro/cart.CXCEDcWV.js
#
# scripts/images.mjs hashes the source bytes together with its encoding recipe,
# so re-shooting a product or changing a quality setting produces a new name and
# a new URL. Astro hashes the cart the same way. A returning buyer gets the new
# file because it is a different file, never because a cache expired.
#
# THE FONTS ARE THE EXCEPTION, AND THEY ARE THE ONE TO BE CAREFUL WITH.
# /fonts/archivo.woff2 and /fonts/jetbrains-mono.woff2 are fixed names with no
# hash. Marking them immutable is a promise these two files are final. It is the
# right trade — they are 75KB together, every page loads both, and nothing about
# a subset font changes on its own — but it means a re-subset MUST ship under a
# new filename and a matching @font-face update. Overwriting either name in
# place leaves every returning buyer on the old file for up to a year, with no
# error anywhere. See FONT-SETUP.md.
# ============================================================================

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
